data.content:
All three code snippets hit EF Core 10 breaking changes. Here's what breaks and the fixes:

---

### 1. `ExecuteUpdateAsync` — no longer accepts expression trees

`ExecuteUpdate`/`ExecuteUpdateAsync` now takes a plain `Func<...>` instead of `Expression<Func<...>>`. Your manual expression tree code **won't compile**.

**Fix** — replace the entire block with:

```csharp
await context.Blogs.ExecuteUpdateAsync(s =>
{
    s.SetProperty(b => b.Views, 8);
    if (nameChanged)
    {
        s.SetProperty(b => b.Name, "foo");
    }
});
```

No more expression tree construction needed.

---

### 2. Complex type column names — two breaking changes

**a) Column uniquification:** `ShippingAddress.Street` and `BillingAddress.Street` previously shared one `Street` column silently. EF 10 auto-appends a number (e.g. `Street1`) to disambiguate. If you have an existing database, this causes a schema mismatch.

**Fix** — pin column names explicitly:

```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<Customer>(b =>
{
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.ShippingAddress,
        p => p.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("Street"));
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.BillingAddress,
        p => p.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("Street"));
});
```

**b) Nested complex types use full path:** `Order.Payment.BillingAddress.City` previously mapped to column `BillingAddress_City`. EF 10 now generates `Payment_BillingAddress_City`.

**Fix** — pin with `HasColumnName` to preserve the old name:

```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<Order>()
    .ComplexProperty(o => o.Payment)
    .ComplexProperty(p => p.BillingAddress)
    .Property(a => a.City)
    .HasColumnName("BillingAddress_City");
```

---

### 3. `IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger` — new `logCommandText` parameter

Every method on this interface now requires an additional `string logCommandText` parameter (for redacted SQL logging).

**Fix** — add the parameter to each method:

```csharp
public class MyLogger : IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger
{
    public InterceptionResult<DbDataReader> CommandReaderExecuting(
        IRelationalConnection connection,
        DbCommand command,
        DbContext context,
        Guid commandId,
        Guid connectionId,
        DateTimeOffset startTime,
        string logCommandText)        // ← new parameter
    {
        // Use logCommandText for logging (sensitive data redacted)
        // Use command.CommandText for actual execution SQL
    }
}
```

Update **all** methods on the interface (`CommandReaderExecuted`, `CommandScalarExecuting`, etc.) the same way.
